# Configure ConnectionStrings:WorkloadsConnection in the host's user secrets before starting.
# For module-local EF commands, configure the same key in Workloads user secrets:
# dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:WorkloadsConnection" "<connection-string>" --project .\Workloads\Workloads.csproj
# From the Workloads directory: dotnet ef database update
# The host also applies pending Workloads migrations at startup.
# Projections are populated asynchronously by Channel events, not by an initial backfill.
# Deleted projections disappear from selection lists; workload history is retained.

@host = https://localhost:7086
@customerId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@employeeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@workloadId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003

### Customer selection: { "customers": [ { "id": "...", "companyName": "..." } ] }
GET {{host}}/workloadcustomers

### Employee selection: { "employees": [ { "id": "...", "givenName": "...", "surname": "..." } ] }
GET {{host}}/workloademployees

### Start: returns id, customerId, employeeId, start (UTC), stop (null), notes.
# Invalid input or missing/deleted customer/employee returns 400.
POST {{host}}/workload
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "employeeId": "{{employeeId}}",
  "notes": "Service work"
}

### Stop: server-generated UTC time. Repeated PUT preserves the first stop time.
# Unknown workload returns 404. Stopping a workload for a deleted projection is allowed.
PUT {{host}}/workload/{{workloadId}}/stop

### History: { "workloads": [ ... ] }, newest first; no matches returns an empty list.
GET {{host}}/workloads/customer/{{customerId}}

### History by employee, including active and stopped workloads.
GET {{host}}/workloads/employee/{{employeeId}}
